Kernel_setRoot
├── when caller is not EntryPoint setRoot
│   └── it should revert with Unauthorized error
└── when caller is EntryPoint or self setRoot
    ├── given the overload setRoot with ValidationId is called
    │   ├── given vId is zero and no fallback validator exists
    │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidRootValidation error
    │   ├── given vId corresponds to an installed validator
    │   │   └── it should set the new root to vId
    │   └── given vId corresponds to an installed permission
    │       └── it should set the new root to vId
    └── given the overload setRoot with Install array is called
        ├── given packages array is empty
        │   └── it should revert with InvalidInitialization error
        ├── given removeCurrent is false
        │   └── it should install packages and set new root without uninstalling current
        ├── given removeCurrent is true
        │   ├── given the current root is a VALIDATOR
        │   │   └── it should uninstall validator and set new root
        │   ├── given the current root is a PERMISSION
        │   │   ├── given uninstallData has incorrect length
        │   │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidDataLength error
        │   │   ├── given uninstallData has correct length
        │   │   │   ├── given policies are not uninstalled in reverse order
        │   │   │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidPermissionUninstallOrder error
        │   │   │   └── given policies are uninstalled in reverse order
        │   │   │       └── it should uninstall permission and set new root
        │   │   └── given the current root is ROOT type
        │   │       └── it should revert with InvalidRootValidation error
        ├── given the first package is not a validator or permission SetRoot
        │   └── it should revert with InvalidRootValidation error
        ├── given the first package moduleType is POLICY
        │   └── it should derive root from permissionId in internalData
        └── given the first package moduleType is SIGNER
            └── it should derive root from permissionId in internalData
